From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:08:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] shell: Panels hide automatically while in tablet mode

While KWin reports tablet mode (org.kde.KWin.TabletModeManager), every panel
is on automatic hide, and each goes back to the person's own setting when
tablet mode ends. A panel keeps two things apart: the visibility mode in
force, which is what the views, the struts and the screen edge use, and the
person's own choice, which is the one that is saved, the one scripting
reads, and the one a change made while in tablet mode goes to. Nothing is
written to the panel's configuration for tablet mode, so a session that ends
in tablet mode leaves every panel as the person set it.

The behaviour is on unless plasmarc says [TabletMode] HidePanels=false; the
General Behavior page has the switch. Without a compositor that answers, or
without a tablet mode, nothing changes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2
